      "message": "I agree that this isn\u0027t a double-free Mutex scenario, but I think this change is required. Based on my analysis, if the reference count is zero in this specific execution path, the state handle and its associated Mutex are cleaned up as expected by \"mdcache_lru_clean()\" function and If the count is positive (refcount \u003e 0), however, it\u0027s probable that the Mutex memory has been corrupted/overwritten. so, I think we should avoid attempting cleanup in this corrupted state,relying instead on the caller \"mdcache_alloc_handle()\" function to safely re-initialize the state handle.",
